   "issue": "The failed first check is kept as its output only: the failed script was overwritten by the fix and is not preserved (no copy or digest), and the rerun, at 22:17:58Z, 47 s after the run's last step and its final clean check, is not in the step log (no command, flags or digest of the fixed script, ef6cc0f5c4da36988044cc8f9f57db01e30b7609e751d7cd6156ac515277cefc). The traceback's line numbers (55, 67, 144, 171, now 56, 68, 145, 172) fit the stated one-line fix but cannot exclude another change of equal length.",
   "required_change": "In the outcome, state that the failed version was not kept, and record the fixed script's SHA-256, the rerun's command, flags and time, and a clean check after it. W2's independent reproduction of every check the script makes supports the result."
  },
  {
   "id": "R-02",
   "severity": "nonmandatory",
   "location": "run-001/doctor.json and its staged portable copy ../OntoKin-local/c271-p34/outcome-staging/run-001/doctor.json",
   "issue": "The doctor's --portable-paths leaves nine distinct paths of the base installation (under <prefix>, which also names its package manager). A9 requires portable copies without machine paths, and the review rules exclude installed-application names.",
   "required_change": "Label the base prefix (for example <prefix>) in the portable copy before commit."
  },
  {
